import Mathlib
import Submission.Work.ClassFieldTower.All
import Submission.Work.ProPDeficiency.All

/-!
# `Work.ShafarevichKoch.RelationBound` -- the Shafarevich--Koch relation bound, isolated

This file isolates **the arithmetic crux**: the classical Shafarevich--Koch theorem describing the
maximal unramified pro-`2` group `G_∅ = Gal(F_∅/F)` of a number field by generators and relations.

## The classical statement

Let `F` be a number field and `G_∅` its maximal unramified pro-`2` extension.  Then (Koch,
*Galois Theory of `p`-Extensions*, Ch. 11 Thm 11.3; Neukirch--Schmidt--Wingberg Cor. 10.7.7;
Shafarevich 1963)

* `d(G_∅) = rank₂ Cl(F)` -- the minimal number of generators is the `2`-rank of the class group
  (this is the "generator half", addressed by `Work.ClassFieldTower.ProTwoGenus` and by the Kummer
  two-descent of this chapter, `Descent.lean`);
* `r(G_∅) - d(G_∅) = df(G_∅) ≤ d₂(O_F^×)` -- the **relation bound**
  (Hajir--Maire--Ramakrishna, arXiv:2103.09508, §1: `0 ≤ df(G_∅) ≤ d(O_K^×)`;
  for an imaginary quadratic field `d₂(O_F^×) = 1`, so `r ≤ d + 1`).

## The encoding used here

A *pro-`2` presentation* of `G_∅` with `d` generators and `r` relations is a tuple of elements
`g_1,…,g_d ∈ G_∅` and of words `w_1,…,w_r` in `d` letters such that

* (`P1`) the kernel of the presentation map `FreeGroup (Fin d) → G_∅`, `x_i ↦ g_i`, is exactly the
  normal closure of the `w_j`; and
* (`P2`) the closed subgroup generated by the `g_i` is all of `G_∅` (equivalently: the `g_i`
  generate every finite quotient of `G_∅`).

This is `HasProTwoPresentation F d r` below, stated without any reference to completions.  It is the
classical input: everything else in the interface consumed by `Work.ClassFieldTower`
(`DescribesMaximalProTwo`, residual `2`-finiteness, minimality of the generating set) is *derived*
from it, see `infiniteProTwoExtension_of_hasProTwoPresentation`.

The remaining gap after this file is exactly the pair `(P1) ∧ (P2)`: the existence of a pro-`2`
presentation with `d = rank₂ Cl(F)` generators and `r ≤ d + d₂(O_F^×)` relations.
-/

set_option linter.style.haveILetI false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

open scoped Classical
open scoped nonZeroDivisors
open scoped NumberField
open NumberField

noncomputable section

namespace Work.ShafarevichKoch

/-- **A pro-`2` presentation of the maximal unramified pro-`2` group.**

`HasProTwoPresentation F d r` says: there is a maximal unramified pro-`2` extension `F_∅` of `F`
with `G_∅ = Gal(F_∅/F)`, elements `g : Fin d → G_∅` and words `w : Fin r → FreeGroup (Fin d)`
such that

* `P1`: the presentation map `FreeGroup (Fin d) → G_∅`, `x_i ↦ g_i`, has kernel the normal closure
  of the words `w_j` (so the abstract group presented is the subgroup of `G_∅` generated by the
  `g_i`);
* `P2`: the closed subgroup generated by the `g_i` is `G_∅` (the `g_i` generate `G_∅`
  topologically).

This is the classical Shafarevich--Koch presentation of `G_∅`; the *numerical* part of the
Shafarevich--Koch theorem is the statement `HasProTwoPresentation F d r` with
`d = rank₂ Cl(F)` and `r ≤ d + d₂(O_F^×)`. -/
def HasProTwoPresentation (F : Type*) [Field F] [NumberField F] (d r : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∃ (M : Work.ClassFieldTower.MaximalUnramifiedProP.{0} F 2)
    (g : Fin d → Work.ClassFieldTower.galoisGroup M) (w : Fin r → FreeGroup (Fin d)),
    MonoidHom.ker (FreeGroup.lift g) = Subgroup.normalClosure (Set.range w) ∧
    (Subgroup.closure (Set.range g)).topologicalClosure = ⊤

/-- The abstract group presented by `d` generators and the words `w`: the quotient
`FreeGroup (Fin d) ⧸ normalClosure (range w)`. -/
abbrev presentedGroup (d r : ℕ) (w : Fin r → FreeGroup (Fin d)) : Type :=
  FreeGroup (Fin d) ⧸ Subgroup.normalClosure (Set.range w)

end Work.ShafarevichKoch
